	"recommendations": {
		"C1": "Add triggers to the word-short axes: UND, OPS, DBG, DAT, ARC, REF.",
		"C2": "Do not add words to TST, REV, IMP: they contain the words and still lose. Add a discriminator ('not for X') or merge the pair.",
		"C3": "Fill or drop the 13 ownerless jobs: B9, C4, D7, D8, I8, I9, Q6, R2, R3, R6, R8, S6, S9.",
		"C4": "Publish strict, adjacent and unrelated owners separately; 'appropriate' hides 25 wrong owners in 106.",
		"C5": "Gate every whenToUse edit on reachability; it costs seconds.",
		"C6": "Author and test lines in the product rendering (name quoted, slug in parentheses, under MODES). Measured 2026-11-23: that form declared 0.778 against 0.500 (extractor v4; 0.714 as first scored), +27.4 points paired (z 3.05), log 40 and 44.",
		"C7": "Do not use list position as a lever: in the product form the last slot declared 19 points less than the same line first.",
		"C8": "Assume the wording effect may be smaller, not larger, in the product form; weight discriminating content over polar phrasing.",
		"C9": "Do not treat field order as a lever. Within the experiment template, swapping slug and name moved nothing (-4.8 points, z -0.52); within the product template the wrong order collapsed the rate to 0.190. Write the product form, in the product order, and do not optimise the order separately.",
		"C10": "Re-run the attribution arms at full size when quota allows: 63 per arm is enough for a 26-point effect, not for a 10-point one.",
		"C11": "Print the display name in the quoted slot: * \"<Name>\" mode (<slug>) - line. One batch, 2026-11-23: name quoted 0.780, slug quoted 0.450, slug quoted with the name in parentheses 0.130. Dropping to a slug-only line saves 761 characters and costs 33 points, so the shorter line is a trade against the routing decision, not a saving (log 43)."
